{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-11-04_ex991earningsrelease2026q3.htm, sha256 6a61807df94a304a57603966f303d53a5ed23e9525ab76791248c3223c213746.\nEX-99.1 2 ex991earningsrelease2026q3.htm EX-99.1 Exhibit 99.1\nMativ Announces Third Quarter 2026 Results\nALPHARETTA, GA, November 4, 2026 -\u2013 Mativ Holdings, Inc. (\"Mativ\" or the \"Company\") (NYSE: MATV) reported financial results for the three-months ended September 30, 2026.\nMativ Third Quarter 2026 Highlights1\n\u2022Sales of $499.5 million decreased 2.8% year over year, and 2.3% on an organic basis, primarily due to the impact of the previously disclosed tornado \u2022GAAP loss of $1.2 million versus GAAP loss of $3.2 million in prior year period; GAAP EPS was $(0.03) \u2022Adjusted income was $17.5 million; Adjusted EPS was $0.31 \u2022Adjusted EBITDA was $62.3 million, down 7% versus prior year period \u2022Year-to-date profitability and cash flow performance pacing ahead of strong prior year \u25e6Gross profit was $295.9 million, up 7% versus prior year \u25e6Cash provided by operating activities was $117.4 million, up 3% versus prior year period \u25e6Free cash flow was $90.5 million, up 5% versus prior year period\nManagement Commentary\n\u201cMativ\u2019s third quarter performance demonstrated continued momentum across the business, highlighted by the FAM segment\u2019s strongest sales growth ever, driven by robust demand in Aerospace & Defense and Transportation,\u201d said Shruti Singhal, Mativ's President and CEO. \u201cOur disciplined execution \u2014 which positioned Mativ to deliver year-over-year third-quarter Adjusted EBITDA growth prior to the operational disruption from the July tornado in Wisconsin \u2014 and our strong cash generation give us confidence in delivering full-year financial performance ahead of the prior year.\n\u201cOur response to the tornado is further proof of Mativ\u2019s resilience and execution capabilities. Recovery remains on plan and we expect inventory losses to be fully recoverable. The team's efforts to quickly restore customer supply have earned strong praise from our customers. I want to thank our crisis management team and all employees for their exceptional customer commitment and dedication while navigating this challenge.\n\u201cWith this solid operational foundation in place, we are pivoting to growth and executing on initiatives that will accelerate sustainable, profitable revenue growth, driving increased customer and shareholder value.\u201d\n1Non-GAAP (or \"adjusted\") measures are reconciled to GAAP measures at the end of this release. Refer to \"Non-GAAP Financial Measures\" for more information.\nMativ Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results\nFiltration & Advanced Materials (FAM) Three Months Ended September 30,\n(in millions; unaudited) 2026 2025 Change 2026 2025\nNet Sales $ 218.5 $ 198.3 $ 20.2\nGAAP Gross Profit & Margin % $ 51.5 $ 42.5 $ 9.0 23.6 % 21.4 %\nAdjusted EBITDA & Margin % $ 39.6 $ 32.9 $ 6.7 18.1 % 16.6 %\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "Filtration & Advanced Materials (FAM) segment sales, comprised primarily of filtration media and components, advanced films, coating and converting solutions, and extruded mesh products, were $218.5 million, up 11.6% on an organic basis, and 10.2% on a reported basis versus the prior year period, reflecting higher volume/mix, including the impact from an exited facility, and higher selling prices.\nAdjusted EBITDA (see non-GAAP reconciliations) of $39.6 million increased 20.4% while Adjusted EBITDA margin of 18.1% increased 150 basis points versus prior year. Higher volume/mix and favorable price vs. cost performance were partially offset by higher manufacturing costs.\nSustainable & Adhesive Solutions (SAS) Three Months Ended September 30,\n(in millions; unaudited) 2026 2025 Change 2026 2025\nNet Sales $ 281.0 $ 315.4 $ (34.4)\nGAAP Gross Profit & Margin % $ 46.2 $ 56.9 $ (10.7) 16.4 % 18.0 %\nAdjusted EBITDA & Margin % $ 32.6 $ 43.3 $ (10.7) 11.6 % 13.7 %\nSustainable & Adhesive Solutions (SAS) segment sales, comprised primarily of tapes, labels, liners, specialty paper, packaging and healthcare solutions, of $281.0 million were down 10.9% versus the prior year period primarily due to the effects of the July tornado incident on our Paper & Packaging business. Lower volume/mix including in Healthcare, and unfavorable currency were partially offset by higher selling prices.\nAdjusted EBITDA (see non-GAAP reconciliations) of $32.6 million decreased 24.7% while Adjusted EBITDA margin of 11.6% decreased 210 basis points compared to the prior year period. Lower volume/mix and higher distribution expenses were partially offset by favorable price vs. cost performance.\nUnallocated Three Months Ended September 30,\n(in millions; unaudited) 2026 2025 Change 2026 2025\nGAAP Operating Expense & % of Sales $ (14.2) $ (14.8) $ 0.6 (2.8) % (2.9) %\nAdjusted EBITDA & % of Sales $ (9.9) $ (9.4) $ (0.5) (2.0) % (1.8) %\nGAAP operating expenses decreased $0.6 million year-over-year, and adjusted unallocated expenses (EBITDA) (see non-GAAP reconciliations) increased $0.5 million versus prior year.\nInterest expense was $18.1 million versus $17.7 million in the prior year period, mainly due to higher average rates on the floating portion of our outstanding debt in 2026.\nOther expense, net was $0.4 million and compared to other expense of $3.9 million in the prior year period. The improvement was primarily attributed to pension costs and foreign currency losses in 2025.\nTax expense was $2.6 million and tax rate was 185.7% for the three months ended September 30, 2026, primarily driven by our geographical earnings mix and our inability to benefit from losses in certain jurisdictions that have a full valuation allowance.\nNon-GAAP Adjustments reflect items included in GAAP gross profit, income, and EPS, but excluded from adjusted results (see non-GAAP reconciliation tables for additional details). The most significant adjustments to the third quarter 2026 results were:\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "\u2022$0.26 per share of purchase accounting expenses (purchase accounting expenses reflect primarily ongoing non-cash intangible asset amortizations associated with mergers and acquisitions) \u2022$0.08 per share of restructuring, restructuring related, and impairment expenses\nCash Flow & Debt\nYear-to-date 2026 cash provided by operating activities was $117.4 million. Capital spending totaled $26.9 million. Working capital was a $11.9 million source of cash due to the impact of an increase in accounts payable and other current liabilities and accrued income taxes, partially offset by an increase in accounts receivable and inventories.\nTotal debt was $976.4 million as of September 30, 2026, an improvement of $52.5 million year-over-year. Cash and cash equivalents was $97.3 million. The resulting net debt was $879.1 million. Total liquidity was approximately $373.5 million, consisting of $97.3 million of Cash and cash equivalents and $276.2 million of revolver availability. The Company's debt is expected to mature on a staggered basis through 2033.\nDividends\nOn November 4, 2026, the Company announced its next quarterly cash dividend of $0.10 per share payable on December 18, 2026 to stockholders of record as of November 27, 2026.\nConference Call\nMativ will hold a conference call to review third quarter 2026 results with investors and analysts at 8:30 a.m. Eastern time on Thursday, November 5, 2026. The earnings conference call will be simultaneously broadcast over the Internet at http://ir.mativ.com. To listen to the call, please go to the Company\u2019s website at least 15 minutes prior to the call to register and to download and install any necessary audio software. For those unable to listen to the live broadcast, a replay will be available on the Company\u2019s website shortly after the call.\nAbout Mativ\nMativ Holdings, Inc. is a global leader in specialty materials, solving our customers\u2019 most complex challenges by engineering bold, innovative solutions that connect, protect and purify our world. Headquartered in Alpharetta, Georgia, we manufacture on three continents and generate sales in over 100 countries through our family of business-to-business and consumer product brands. The company\u2019s two operating segments, Filtration & Advanced Materials and Sustainable & Adhesive Solutions, target premium applications across diversified and growing categories. Our broad portfolio of technologies combines polymers, fibers and resins to optimize the performance of our customers\u2019 products across multiple stages of the value chain. Our leading positions are a testament to our best-in-class global manufacturing, supply chain and materials science capabilities. We drive innovation and enhance performance, finding potential in the impossible.\nForward-Looking Statements\n"}
